MMC99 @MMC99_VERSION@ - a C99 compiler for Linux and Windows programs

Unpack this folder anywhere. Nothing else needs to be installed:

    tar -xzf MMC99-@MMC99_VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz

Compile and run a program:

    MMC99/bin/MMC99 hello.c -o hello
    ./hello

Build the same program for Windows:

    MMC99/bin/MMC99 --target=x86_64-w64-windows-gnu hello.c -o hello.exe

MMC99 runs on x86-64 Linux with glibc 2.34 or newer, libstdc++ and zlib:
Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12 and later have all three. The Linux programs it
builds need glibc 2.34 or newer too.

To type MMC99 from any folder, add MMC99/bin to PATH.
"MMC99 --help" lists every option.

MMC99 compiles all of C99 and uses each system's own C library: glibc on
Linux, MinGW-w64's on Windows, with all of their headers, windows.h included.
A header that needs an extension MMC99 does not support fails with an error
message; MMC99 never builds a wrong program from it.

CONFORMANCE.md documents every choice C99 leaves to the compiler, and every
extension. SOURCES.txt says where every file comes from; licenses holds their
licenses.
